# Declared in frameworks/base/core/java/android/companion/virtual/flags/flags.aconfig
# Computer control for Quire (ANAL-216, docs/quire.md §2.4): VirtualDeviceManager's requestComputerControlSession, the
# ACCESS_COMPUTER_CONTROL permission, and the platform's safety paths for it (launch warnings for automated apps, the
# undismissable session notification, Settings' "Screen automation" page). Enabled in trunk_staging, not in cp2a.
# The flags cp2a already enables with it: computer_control_consent, _role_assistant_requirement,
# _activity_policy_strict, _user_restriction, _managed_profiles, _config_change_override.
flag_value {
  package: "android.companion.virtualdevice.flags"
  name: "computer_control_access"
  state: ENABLED
  permission: READ_ONLY
}
